\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces CATCH training and one-trajectory inference. A Haar transform maps the voided image to eight subbands, concatenated with noisy target subbands and a signed mask. WavUNet predicts clean coefficients; inverse transformation and hard compositing restore the observed region. Selected random and weighted-mixture pipelines repeat this path five times and aggregate voxel-wise; fixed mask uses $N=1$. Thumbnails were selected without reconstruction metrics.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:catch-architecture}{{1}{3}{CATCH training and one-trajectory inference. A Haar transform maps the voided image to eight subbands, concatenated with noisy target subbands and a signed mask. WavUNet predicts clean coefficients; inverse transformation and hard compositing restore the observed region. Selected random and weighted-mixture pipelines repeat this path five times and aggregate voxel-wise; fixed mask uses $N=1$. Thumbnails were selected without reconstruction metrics}{figure.1}{}}
